  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats delivered a fifteen-song set on March 2, 2004, at The First Unitarian Church in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania [1]. This performance is the fifty-fifth show in the archive’s collection for the band, following a previous appearance at Will’s Pub on February 20, 2004 [2]. The available recording is a single audience capture that lasts fifty-six minutes [1]. The setlist opens with “Mole,” which is the earliest version of that song in the archive [1]. Other tracks include “Southwood Plantation Road,” “Linda Blair Was Born Innocent,” and “International Small Arms Traffic Blues” [1]. The band performed “Feed This End,” a rare song with only three archived performances, marking its first appearance in forty-one archived shows [1]. “It Froze Me,” “Jaipur,” and “Tallahassee” follow in the sequence [1]. “Neon Orange Glimmer Song” and “California Song” are also featured, with the latter being a bustout in thirty-seven archived shows [1]. The set continues with “Shadow Song,” “Cotton,” and “Quito” [1]. The performance concludes with “See America Right” and “Going to Georgia” [1]. This audience recording is the only available capture of this specific date [1].",
